# TTS Platform — AI Coding Agent Build Specification

## 0. Mission

Build a production-ready, extensible **AI Text-to-Speech SaaS platform** focused on creators, businesses, and developers.

The platform must provide:

- High-quality text-to-speech generation
- Free, Standard, Premium, Ultra/Premium+ voice tiers
- User-owned private custom/clone voices
- Voice cloning with explicit authorization/consent safeguards
- Projects and long-form scripts
- Generation history and versioning
- MP3/WAV export
- Subscription plans and usage/credit accounting
- A fair-use "Unlimited" plan
- Developer API and API keys
- Usage analytics
- Admin dashboard
- Provider/model abstraction so TTS providers can be swapped without rewriting the application
- Background job processing
- Audio storage and lifecycle management
- Strong security, rate limiting, audit logging, and abuse prevention

The product should feel like a professional **AI Voice Studio**, not merely a text box that calls a TTS API.

---

# 1. Non-Negotiable Engineering Rules

1. Use TypeScript on the web frontend.
2. Use Python/FastAPI for the backend and AI/audio services.
3. Use PostgreSQL as the source of truth for relational data.
4. Use Redis for caching, rate limiting, queues, and ephemeral job state.
5. Use background workers for TTS, cloning, audio processing, and other expensive operations.
6. Never block an HTTP request while waiting for a long TTS generation.
7. Store audio in object storage (S3-compatible storage such as Cloudflare R2 or AWS S3), not PostgreSQL.
8. Never hard-code a single TTS vendor into application/business logic.
9. Implement a provider adapter interface from day one.
10. Track usage and estimated provider cost for every generation.
11. Treat "Unlimited" as **fair-use unlimited**, never literal infinite compute.
12. Never expose provider API keys to the browser.
13. Never expose private voice IDs/data belonging to another user.
14. Every state-changing sensitive action must be authenticated and authorized server-side.
15. All webhook endpoints must verify provider signatures.
16. All billing/usage mutations must be idempotent.
17. Do not log raw user voice samples or sensitive audio URLs unnecessarily.
18. Voice cloning must include explicit authorization/rights confirmation and abuse controls.
19. Build tests alongside features; do not leave testing until the end.
20. Prefer simple, maintainable architecture over premature microservices.

