# 11. TTS Generation Workflow

Frontend:

```text
User enters text
↓
Selects voice
↓
Selects settings
↓
Clicks Generate
```

Backend:

```text
Validate authentication
↓
Validate entitlement
↓
Validate text
↓
Calculate usage
↓
Reserve usage/credit
↓
Create generation(status=queued)
↓
Create background job
↓
Return generation_id
```

Worker:

```text
Load generation
↓
Mark processing
↓
Resolve voice
↓
Resolve provider/model
↓
Call provider
↓
Validate returned audio
↓
Normalize/transcode with FFmpeg if needed
↓
Upload to object storage
↓
Record duration/cost/provider request ID
↓
Mark completed
↓
Finalize usage
```

On failure:

```text
Retry transient errors
↓
If final failure
↓
Refund reserved usage where appropriate
↓
Mark failed
↓
Record safe error
```

---

# 12. Long Text Handling

Do not send arbitrarily huge text to one provider request.

Implement chunking.

Example:

```text
10,000 characters
↓
split into safe chunks
↓
generate chunk 1
generate chunk 2
...
↓
validate each chunk
↓
concatenate
↓
normalize
↓
final output
```

Preserve:

- paragraph order
- pauses
- sentence boundaries where possible
- voice/settings consistency

Store chunk-level job state so failed chunks can retry independently.

