# 16. Voice Cloning

Build cloning as a separate workflow.

### Upload flow

```text
Create Clone
↓
Upload audio
↓
Validate file type
↓
Validate duration
↓
Validate size
↓
Analyze audio quality
↓
Show rights/consent confirmation
↓
User confirms authorization
↓
Queue clone job
↓
Clone provider/model
↓
Quality check
↓
Create private voice
```

Supported source formats can include:

- WAV
- MP3
- M4A where supported

Set configurable limits.

Example configuration:

```text
max_upload_size_mb
min_duration_seconds
max_duration_seconds
allowed_mime_types
```

Do not embed fixed business limits throughout code.

## Consent

Before cloning, require the user to confirm that:

- they own the voice, or
- they have authorization to clone it, and
- they have the necessary rights to use the generated voice.

Record:

```text
consent_confirmed
rights_confirmed
timestamp
policy_version
```

For higher-risk workflows, provide additional review/verification mechanisms.

## Default privacy

All cloned voices:

```text
private = true
```

User must explicitly publish a voice if marketplace functionality is later enabled.

